nsettled."}, {"turn": 24, "text": "Opus 5.5's C6 matched the engine's first choice and moved the lead from -7.0 to -7.7. It sat directly under Black's C7 stone, and the position after it was the best White had all game."}, {"turn": 28, "text": "D5 was Opus 5.5's worst move, losing 3.8 points and taking the lead from -7.9 to -4.1. The engine wanted E6. Black took E6 next, and the margin stayed near 4 points to the end."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py only flood-fills groups and counts their liberties on a pasted board, and count.py only does an area count of the current position; neither chooses or ranks moves nor looks ahead. The other commands were cat/tail of notes and a Python edit and append to CLAUDE.md and games.md, which is record-keeping.", "stop": false}}